{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1785240781,"nonce":"Fk7bfuagPRwYuZTyQiorVTgFijU=","target":"d23222b707b5c4141e5198f45b213c487719904493faa579e99ebddaa4777c42","message":"Reported by Mark Brown on IRC, 2026-07-27. Mark went looking for a way\nto unarchive a series in b4 review and found there isn't one, which is\na problem when a submitter keeps sending an already-archived series.\nIn his case it was a cross-tree series: he acked the parts for his\nsubsystem, the maintainer who was supposed to apply the rest dropped\nthe ball, and the series came back after he had archived it.\n\nArchiving a series is currently a one-way door. What archive does today\n(review_tui/_tracking_app.py, _archive_branch):\n\n- tars up cover.txt + tracking.js + patches.mbx into\n  $XDG_DATA_HOME/b4/review-archived/\u003cchange_id\u003e.tar.gz\n- deletes the b4/review/\u003cchange_id\u003e branch\n- keeps the DB row but sets status='archived'\n- marks the series accepted+archived in Patchwork\n\nThe tracking list filters out archived rows unconditionally, and there\nis no action, CLI or TUI, to bring one back.\n\nThe dead end gets actively misleading when the submitter resends. In\ncmd_track (review/tracking.py), the archived row still matches by\nchange-id / fingerprint / revision catalog, so:\n\n- a resend with a new revision gets folded into the invisible archived\n  row, and b4 says \"Upgrade the series in the review TUI to the new\n  version\" -- impossible, since the series is not shown in the TUI and\n  its review branch no longer exists;\n- an identical resend exits with \"This series is already tracked\n  (status: archived)\".\n\nEither way the new posting is swallowed and the user has no way forward\nshort of hand-editing the SQLite database.\n\nNote: \"a v+1 after archive is ignored\" is deliberate -- it is the\npartial+done flow settled in bug a01c5b5. This entry is not about\nchanging that default; it is about the missing escape hatch for when\nthe \"no new versions after archive\" assumption turns out to be wrong\n(cross-tree ball-drops, submitters resending applied series, or plain\narchive-by-mistake).\n\nProposed scope:\n\n1. An explicit unarchive path: a \"show archived\" toggle in the tracking\n   list plus an Unarchive action that restores the previous status and\n   review branch. The tarball contains everything needed (patches.mbx +\n   tracking.js, including the pre-archive status); alternatively the\n   thread can be re-fetched from lore since all msgids survive in the\n   DB. Should also clear the archived flag in Patchwork.\n\n2. Fix the cmd_track dead end: when the matched row is archived and a\n   genuinely new revision is discovered, either offer to reactivate the\n   series or at least print instructions that actually work.\n\nWorkaround for now: flip the row manually with\n  sqlite3 $XDG_DATA_HOME/b4/review/\u003cid\u003e.db \\\n    \"UPDATE series SET status='waiting' WHERE change_id='...'\"\nThe series reappears in the TUI and 'u' picks up the resend; the old\nreview branch stays gone but is not needed to review the new posting.","files":null}]}